A||||5||GT Bastard||Anybody got a 3.2 with NOS?||||5||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||11-04-2001||11:35 PM||||If so, what pistons are you running?  I'm curious if anyone has ventured to throw NOS at the hypereutectic pistsons yet...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/icare.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shaun41178||11-05-2001||01:36 AM||||To be totally honest with you I think the hyper pistons will do just fine.  They are stronger then cast pistons without a doubt.  And I was running a 70 shot for 3 years and a 90 shot once and the stockers did just fine.  The hypers should be able to handle a 70 shot no problem.<P>You are just going to have to make sure that there is enough fuel to keep from leaning out.  I think many people get hyper pistons when running nitrous thinking they are stronger but then forget about the fuel and run them lean and burn them up cause they try and run more nitrous cause they have stronger pistons.<P>Just remember that the Lt-1 engines in late model camarobirds have hyper pistons from teh factory and people drop a 125 shot on them.  Something to think about.<P>I think you will be fine.  just don't go overboard<P><P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||11-05-2001||10:49 AM||||Not sure... I was reading an archive about Nitrous in the car ( <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010924-1-006347.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010924-1-006347.html</A>  ) and I did notice this:<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR><B>Sure...also tell them my 100hp makes 100hp and 200ft/lbs of TORQUE. You can use 100-150hp (if you have forged pistons...NO HYPERUTECTICS (sp?), too much silicone...can't handle the increased cylinder pressure. Even NOS doesn't like them for nitrous)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It appears to really only apply if you're running a huge shot, but still something to consider.  I someday hope to have a Nitrous Kit (Wet if I can afford it) on my 3.1L  ...someday...<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||11-05-2001||01:31 PM||||They can't handle the increased cylinder pressure?  So they can't handle lots of boost either?  It seems like I've seen a lot of boosted cars that claim to use hyper pistons...  I've already got the fuel to keep up with the NOS, but I don't want to take chances.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/icare.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shaun41178||11-05-2001||03:07 PM||||They can handle increased cylinder pressure just fine.  Like I said just don't go overboard.  Go with a 70 shot and you should be fine.<P>The reason for the higher silicon in the pistons is to keep thermal temps stable and lower throughout the piston.  Also to keep the piston from shrinking and expanding too much.  Forged pistons have less silicon but they also have more clearence when cold so there will be more piston slap and increased wear with a lot of cold startups.  Forged pistons expand more then hyper and stock pistons.<P>I say go for it.  I am sure they can handle a 70 shot no prob but if you feel it won't go with a 50 shot.  Thats like 8 extra hp per cylinder.  Thats not that much.  You say you will have enough fuel so you should be safe.  <P>I had hyper pistons when I was doing a 3.2 buildup.  Used the same ones that everyone else seems to use.  I was planning on running a 100 shot on them and wasn't worried about blowing through them from the cylinder pressure.  Ended up selling everything to GT GT 87 (Steve)||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||11-05-2001||03:13 PM||||I'd agree... unless you're going overboard (150 shot)- a normal shot (70, even 100) should be fine with the hyper's.  <P>If still in doubt, contact the manufacturer/supplier of your Nitrous Kit (whether it be NOS, Nitrous Xpress, Venom, ZEX, etc...) and explain to them what you're expecting to do- and if they think the hyper pistons will hold up OK.  Then <B>Go For It!</B>||||reg||1
